 2. Luigi Mangione pleads guilty 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Luigi Mangione stands between his attorneys, Karen Friedman Agnifilo and Marc Agnifilo, in Manhattan Criminal Court today. Courtroom sketch: Jane Rosenberg via AP 🏛️ Luigi Mangione pleaded guilty today in federal court to stalking charges tied to the 2024 killing of UnitedHealthcare CEO Brian Thompson , Axios' Donica Phifer and Avery Lotz write. 

 Mangione, 28, told the court : "On the morning of December 4, 2024, I shot Mr. Thompson in Manhattan, and he died." Mangione faced a potential life sentence if convicted in a federal trial.

 The guilty plea could mean his lawyers ask to dismiss separate state charges, including second-degree murder. 🗓️ What's next: His sentencing is scheduled for Dec. 18.

 The judge told Mangione he will still be required to serve at least 85% of his sentence for the federal charges. 👀 What we're watching: Mangione is still facing a trial in New York state court next month.

 He has pleaded not guilty to all eight state charges in New York. He could face a life sentence if convicted. Share this story ... Timeline of events . 

 
 
