 4. 📚 1 fun thing: Dorm decor 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 College dorms are becoming customized, social-media-ready micro-apartments, Axios' Josephine Walker writes .

 Why it matters: Dorm rooms are tiny. The decor economy is not. 💵 The "designer dorm" industry — which includes decked-out rooms worth thousands — has grown alongside viral TikTok dorm tours and hauls.

 Parents are also trying to make their child's transition to college easier. 🥊 Reality check: The market looks wildly different depending on which side of the Mason-Dixon line your campus sits.

 ⭐ In SEC country, dorm rooms are often personalized with monograms and items reflecting school spirit. 🚚 In the Northeast , dorm design can be couture, but the biggest luxury is having someone else wrestle with a U-Haul on a cramped city street. Go deeper . 

 
 
